Subject: Zeroes the register area and puts `undefined` only where a value can be observed

What this does
  Zeroes the register area and puts `undefined` only where a value can be observed.

Why we need it
  The frame filled every register with `undefined`, that literal form is unsound, because the fill is load-bearing for the store handlers' old-value release.

What it adds
  The fill becomes `memset` followed by `undefined` only for the registers the analysis marks as possibly read before written; a NULL list still means fill-all, which is what every blob function gets; the list is used only when it covers under half the range.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
